# 080 · A button says at once that it took, and shows its outcome without a refresh

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics · **Depends on:** [063](063-scan-and-steer.goal)

## What

A dashboard button that sends something to a rig says at once that the click took, then shows the progress until the outcome, without a refresh:

- **Run it** on a rig's checks: the button turns at once into a disabled **Sending…**. When control has queued the command, the check's chip says `sent`, and the line under its name says `Sent to the rig at 03:41 UTC. It starts when the rig takes it.` When the rig takes it, the chip says `running` with the time so far, such as `running · 1 m 12 s`, and the line says what the check pauses. When `rig_check_finished` arrives, the row shows the result in place. A refusal, a failed or an expired command says so in words, and the button comes back.
- Every other button with the same gap gets the same pattern: each signed command's button, a message to the agents, **Use** on Providers, **Update to** a version and the buttons of a rig that control set up, **Save changes** on **Edit rig**, and **Start a run**.

## Why

The owner, on 2026-10-21: "When I click run it I get no indication that it accepted, its running. I have to wait a bit and then refresh to see if its running."

Control already knew each command's state (pending, delivered, failed, expired) and when the rig's report with it came; the page did not show it until a refresh.

## Done when

- [x] Control answers a form sent by the page's script in JSON, with the route that says how the action stands: a command, a rig check's row, a rig taking a model, an update and a change to a rig that control set up. Each answers a state in words, whether it is final, and whether the page loads again (a started run).
- [x] The page's script (served with `/ui/assets/app.js`) sends the form, follows its route every 2 seconds (5 after two minutes), and draws again the parts of the page that changed (`data-part`), but not one the owner is typing in. Times count on each second.
- [x] A rig check's row: not run yet, sent, running with its time, passed or failed, refused or expired with the reason, also when the rig ran the check by itself.
- [x] Without the script, every form posts as before, and the page it lands on says `Sent to <rig> at <time> UTC.`
- [x] Tests: the script's parts that touch no page run against control's own answers; the follow routes; the no-script path; a real harness takes each command through the supervisor's relay.
- [x] The pages that describe the buttons, and those that said to refresh after them, match.

## Decisions

- **2026-10-21:** No server-sent events: a small poll of routes over control's own store, which control already has. No new store tables.
- **2026-10-21:** The page draws again marked parts only, never the whole page: parts with listeners of their own stay as they are, and Live's ☰ and the experiment queue's drag now listen on the document.
- **2026-10-21:** A command is done when the rig's signed report with it reaches control: the page then shows the change.

## Open questions

- The sidebar's campaign and rig lines are not drawn again: goal 077 rebuilds that navigation.

## Progress

- 2026-10-21: Built. Run it, Check, every signed command's button, the message box, Use, Update to, the buttons of a rig set up by control, Save changes on Edit rig and Start a run follow their action to its outcome. Checked in a browser against a local control with a real harness.

